{{also|Dutchman}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{m|en|Dutchman}}. Attested mainly in the US from the late 19th century.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|En-us-dutchman.ogg|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|en-uk-dutchman.ogg|a=UK}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|dutchmen}}

# {{lb|en|carpentry|masonry}} A piece of [[wood]] or [[stone]] used to repair a larger piece, shaped such that it fills as exactly as possible a [[void]] or [[cavity]] that is to be repaired.
# A [[flaw]] or void repaired with such a piece.
# {{lb|en|theater}} A [[cloth]] [[strip]] attached to a [[flat]] to conceal a joint.
# {{lb|en|nautical}} {{ellipsis of|en|Flying Dutchman|nodot=a}}: a {{l|en|ghost ship}}

